  💭 The lowest *bits* bits of *code*, the other way round. Deflate writes the codes
  💭 that stand for bytes from their highest bit, and everything else from its lowest.
  🐇 🔒❗️ 🔄 code 🔢 bits 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 🍇
    0 ➡️ 🖍🆕turned
    code ➡️ 🖍🆕left
    0 ➡️ 🖍🆕done
    🔁 done ◀️ bits 🍇
      🤜turned 👈 1🤛 💢 🤜left ⭕ 1🤛 ➡️ 🖍turned
      left 👉 1 ➡️ 🖍left
      done ➕ 1 ➡️ 🖍done
    🍉
    ↩️ turned
  🍉

  📗
    *data* as a gzip stream: what `gzip -dc` turns back into *data*. The
    stream is at most an eighth longer than *data*, and 20 bytes.
